ED_DATE x 3 5cm and is located in the lateral half of the specimen  and an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm area in the medial aspect of the specimen  No prior biopsy site or discrete masses are identified in this specimen  Representative sections of fibrous tissue are submitted from lateral to medial in cassettes C L with cassettes G and H corresponding to tissue from the center of the specimen  No lymph nodes are identified within the specimen  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 8 4cm unremarkable skin ellipse on the anterior surface of the specimen with a 3 0cm in diameter areola with a 1 2cm in diameter x 0 5cm in nipple which is grossly unremarkable  There is a stitch in the superior or 12 o clock aspect of the specimen as per the surgeons  note on the requisition form  The anterior resection margin is blue inked and the posterior resection margin is black inked  The specimen is sectioned along the supero inferior access from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink mass located in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen  The remainder of the specimen consists of adipose tissue with firm tan fibrotic areas throughout  Throughout the fibrous tissue as far as 7 0cm away from the main mass there are numerous   REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm in diameter tan pink nodule  The main mass is REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm away from the closest resection margin which is the posterior margin 3 5cm away from the lateral edge of the specimen and 4 5cm from the superior aspect of the specimen  Two nodular soft tissue fragments are disected as the lateral aspect of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows  M  Unremarkable medial breast tissue  N S  Fibrous tissue with pink nodules  submitted from medial to lateral toward the mass with the specimen submitted in cassette O  coming from tissue 7 0cm away from the mass  T W  Sections of the mass with posterior margin in cassettes T  U and V  X  Unremarkable lateral breast tissue  Y  A single bisected axillary nodule  Z  A whole axillary nodule  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fibrofatty tissue  part of which are dissected for nodular soft tissue fragments grossly resembling lymph nodes  which range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The two largest nodules are each bisected and individually submitted in cassettes AA BB  The remaining two nodules are submitted while in cassettes CC  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  CARCINOMA IS NOT IDENTIFIED  AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORK UP  O R  Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D  BREAST LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION , Unchecked.
