agnosis of a lesion in the left breast     Clinical History  57 year old female history of left breast cancer  status post  radiation  now with thickening along surgical scar     Physical Exam  The left breast showed a 1 0cm tender ill defined irregular  hard fix mass with overlying skin puckering     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     3 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   2 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by Roseann Wu  MD    Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  Krista Elliott  NP was notified of the preliminary results by phone at  11 50 am           The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Martha Bishop Pitman MD on REMOVED_DATE 13 39       Hormone Receptor Quantitation  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   Some tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 protein     Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuc