Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 12 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE TUBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  SEVERELY ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MINUTE FOCUS ASSOCIATED WITH INVASIVE COMPONENT  PRESENT  0 1 CM FROM AN INKED MARGIN  3  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal breast parenchyma with a firm area of fibrosis corresponding to the x ray findings  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A H  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  BENIGN  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 50 CLINICAL DATA  59 year old Asian female  status post ultrasound guided core biopsy   right breast ovoid hypoechoic solid mass at 9 o clock  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm    fibroadenoma versus carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES  DIFFUSE LARGE B CELL LYMPHOMA  NOTE  Sections show a dense diffuse infiltrate of medium sized and large atypical lymphoid cells with oval or slightly irregular nuclei  prominent nucleoli and scant cytoplasm  Mitoses are frequent  Occasional tingible body macrophages are present  The histologic features are consistent with lymphoma and immunostains support the diagnosis   See addendum   Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 07                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains  kappa  lambda  there is monotypic cytoplasm  Ig kappa  staining of many lymphoid cells in a diffuse pattern  With antibodies to B lineage antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibodies to T lineage associated antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of rare small cells scattered within the tissue  With antibody to cytokeratin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 cam 5 2  there is no staining of tumor cells  The cells are also positive for bcl 2 and many are positive for bcl 6  Overall  approximately 70  of the tumor cells stain for Ki 67  proliferation   Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of diffuse large B cell lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast   are multiple cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A and B  Gross Description by  JULIE ZWIRBLE Resident  MINDY J  HULL  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Diane R Fingold  M D  Helenanne D alessandro  M D  John Henry Eichhorn  M D  Lan Wang  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSIES , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  18 MAY 94 at 11 45 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  PHYLLOIDES TUMOR  LOW GRADE  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN A TINY FOCUS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 8cm in greatest dimension and displays moderate stromal cellularity  In regions  the tumor has an infiltrative border  and the tumor cells extend to the margin of the specimen in one small area  The tumor cells do not show either atypia or mitotic activity  Stromal overgrowth is not present  These findings suggest a low likelihood for recurrence and metastasis  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 MAY 94 at 12 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a fairly well demarcated lesion  REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in maximum dimension and extending to within 1mm of the inked margin  The lesion is tan gray  bulging and mobile  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  submitted in cassette L  A section representing the lesion with the closest margin is submitted in cassette A  the lesion in cassettes B through G  remainder of the specimen is cassettes H through K  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  FAVOR BENIGN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Christopher S Ogilvy  M D  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
