Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 3 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 44 year old woman with a history of invasive ductal carcinoma with lymph node metastasis  She is status post neoadjuvant therapy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH TUMOR REGRESSION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE TABLE 1  B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION 1  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA INVOLVING SIX OF FOURTEEN LYMPH NODES  6 14   2  TUMOR REGRESSION IS PRESENT  SEE TABLE 2 C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  D  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  gross and microscopic   The invasive carcinoma is present as discrete small nests of tumor cells in a background of fibrosis and granulation tissue  T he findings are interpreted as tumor regression secondary to prior neoadjuvant therapy  The size of the tumor measured by gross and microscopic examination is an estimate which reflects the area of fibrosis involved by tumor  GRADE  3  Neoadjuvant therapy limits the grading  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOM