ins a small amount of brown  semi fluid substance  The adjacent parenchyma is composed of focally hemorrhagic  firm  white  fibrous tissue which extends to the overlying nipple  The biopsy cavity does not grossly involve the nipple  The biopsy site comes within 1 0cm of the closest superoanterior margin  3 5cm from the closest inferior margin  3 5cm from the closest medial margin  and 4 5cm from the closest lateral margin  The remaining parenchyma is composed of predominately fatty  unremarkable tissue  Minimal wisps of fibrous tissue are identified  No additional lesions are seen  There is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm attached portion of axillary fat  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  The highest axillary lymph node is identified by a suture  The lymph nodes range from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  SECTION CODE  A   Indurated nipple in relation to biopsy cavity  B C  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest deep inked resection margin  D E  Further representative sections of biopsy cavity  including areas of fat necrosis and overlying scar  F   Biopsy cavity with adjacent  indurated  focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue  G   Representative section of unremarkable  minimally fibrous parenchyma from lateral aspect  H   Highest axillary sutured lymph node  bisected and entirely submitted  I M  Representative sections of remaining lymph node  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
