Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 96 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 96 at 13 09 CLINICAL DATA  71 year old woman with left breast infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN FOUR OF TWENTY LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTRANODAL EXTENTION IN ONE LYMPH NODE AND PERINODAL LYMPHATIC INVOLVEMENT IN ONE LYMPH NODE  2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SEVERAL FOCI ADJACENT TO HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY   SEE NOTE   3  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FOCAL LACTATIONAL CHANGE  6  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Margins appear free of carcinoma  LYMPH NODE  LEVEL I   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 MAY 96 at 14 39                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  and unit number are two containers  Labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen including a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  A REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse contains a centrally located 3 5cm unremarkable areola with an unremarkable 1 0cm in greatest dimension nipple in its center  Infero lateral to the nipple complex  is a 4 0cm healing oblique surgical incision which comes within 1 2cm of the inferior skin ellipse resection margin  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm blood and filled biopsy cavity with sutures located 2 0cm from the nearest  deep and inferior  resection margins  Tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity is tan white and semi firm to firm  The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable with no areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Section code  A  biopsy cavity in relation to inked deep resection margin B  biopsy cavity in relation to inked inferior resection margin C F  representative sections of biopsy cavity G  representative section of semi firm breast tissue from medial portion of breast H  representative section of prior surgical incision I  representative section of nipple Dissection of the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm attached axillary tail reveals numerous soft tan to semi firm lymph nodes measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  submitted in J M  Labeled  Level 1 node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm massive fatty tissue containing a single 1 0cm tan semi firm lymph node  bissected and submitted entirely in N  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  David L Berger  M D  PART A  LEVEL 1 NODE PART B  LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
