laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm sheet of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple surgical staples and accompanied with an x ray and a localizing wire within one partially detached fragment at the periphery of the specimen  A 0 8cm nodule is palpable near the localizing wire and a second 0 6cm nodule is palpable in the main part of the specimen  Both nodules are within 0 2cm of the surface of the specimen  The nodule of the periphery of the specimen is white tan on cross section and is submitted in cassettes A and B entirely  Adjacent breast tissue is submitted in cassettes C and D  The central nodule has a red tan cut surface and is consistent with a lymph node and is submitted entirely in cassette E  the remaining breast tissue is sectioned revealing several lymph nodes and is submitted in cassettes F through EE  entirely  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Checked.
