mitted as follows  D  Medial margin  entirely  E  Lateral margin  entirely  F G  Posterior margin  representative  closest  H  Inferior  I  Anterior  J  Superior  K  Tumor  center  R  Additional inferior margin  Labeled  posterior margin right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm yellow tan  irregular  fibrofatty tissue fragment that is inked in black  serially sectioned and entirely submitted as L  Labeled  inferior margin right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue that is marked by a stitch on one side  The stitched surface is inked black  the opposite surface is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as M and N  Also received is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow tan  unmarked soft tissue fragment that is inked in black  bisected  and entirely submitted as O  Labeled  final shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue fragments that are inked in black and entirely submitted as P through Q  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Frozen section diagnoses  1 and 2 Lymph nodes  right axillary sentinel   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  SOUHAD YOUNES  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR MARGIN   PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN   PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS   PART E  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 59 CLINICAL DATA  57 year old with bilateral breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM AND INVOLVING A SCLEROSING PAPILLARY NODULE  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  CAPILLARY HEMANGIOMA  SKIN  NOTE  Ductal carcinoma in situ focally extends to the margin of the specimen  While the sclerosis makes assessment for invasion difficult  no definite stromal  lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The carcinoma in situ is not associated with the biopsy cavity and represents a separate lesion  No residual carcinoma in situ is identified in the region of the biopsy cavity  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3   SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Carcinoma extends 0 2cm from the lateral margin  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The carcinoma is distant from the prior biopsy site and represents a separate lesion  No residual carcinoma is identified in the region of the prior excision site  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN 2 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Carcinoma completely replaces two lymph nodes with transgression of the capsule focally in both nodes  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is an unoriented simple mastectomy specimen measuring 21 x 14 x 4 5cm  There is an overlying wrinkled  tan skin ellipse which has a 1 0cm retracted nipple  At one end of the skin ellipse  there is a 3 8cm well healed surgical incision  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm pink purple papule that approaches one skin margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm biopsy cavity which is fibrotic and hemorrhagic  The surrounding tissue shows fat necrosis  This biopsy cavity is located 1 5cm from the deep margin  No residual tumor is grossly appreciated  Further sectioning of the breast reveals yellow fatty tissue with a moderate amount of gray white fibrous tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  gray white nodule located 3 5cm from the skin margin  6 5cm from the biopsy cavity and grossly appears to approach the inked margin  No other lesions are grossly appreciated or palpated  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity to deep margin  B E  Biopsy cavity  H  Additional firm gray white lesion  totally submitted  I  Skin with papule  J K  Random sections of remaining breast parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is the product of a left modified radical mastectomy REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm with an attached 17 x 10 x 3cm axillary tail  The overlying  wrinkled  tan skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 7 8cm  There is a 4 0cm well healed surgical incision in the inferolateral aspect located 0 5cm from the skin margin  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibrotic and hemorrhagic biopsy cavity with surrounding fat necrosis  This biopsy cavity is located 1 0cm from the skin margin  0 8cm from the deep margin  and 0 5cm from the inferior margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast reveals predominantly yellow fatty tissue and a moderate amount of gray white fibrous tissue  There are two  firm  gray white nodules measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm and  7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  These two foci are located in the lateral aspect of the specimen 4 5cm from the superior skin margin  6 0cm to the cavity  No other lesions are grossly appreciated or palpated  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The lymph nodes are focally cystic  Further sections are submitted as follows  L  Biopsy cavity to deep end  M N  Biopsy cavity to inferior margin  O  Biopsy cavity to skin  P Q  Nodules entirely submitted  R S  Random sections of remaining breast tissue  T V  Lymph nodes  W  From one lymph node  X  Representative sections of one lymph node  bisected  Y  Representative sections from one lymph node  bisected  Z AA  Representative sections of one lymph node  bisected  BB DD  Representative sections from large lymph node  trisected  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
