r of the breast parenchyma is composed of grossly unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  Section code  A B  representative sections of mass C  closest deep margin D E  representative sections of firm  focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue surrounding the mass F  representative section of adjacent nodular firm fibrous tissue G  representative section of overlying skin Within the axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 6cm in greatest dimension are identified  Representative lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes H L  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 46 CLINICAL DATA  Prior lumpectomy and radiation therapy 16 years ago  now with a new lump in a separate quadrant  which was found to be cancerous by core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SEVERAL DUCTS WITHIN THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  Note  The resection margins are free of tumor  No lymphotic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 28 Proofread by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a simple mastectomy specimen  with skin ellipse measuring 5 x 2 5cm and a grossly unremarkable nipple  The breast itself measures 8 x 4 x 5cm  Sectioning reveals a stellate  ill defined lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  which is firm and more than 2cm from the closest inked margins  SECTION CODE A D  Stellate lesion submitted in toto  E G  Representative sections of breast parenchyma  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
