Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Olga Kolman  M D  Signed Out by  Elena F Brachtel  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  New subtle right architectural distortion  right breast  History of left breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCAL DENSE FIBROSIS  SEE TABLE  SEE NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Scattered tumor cells spanning an area of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm on two slides   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    GRADE  2 LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma is less than 0 1cm away from the anterior margin along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  REMOVED_DATE MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ is less than 0 1cm from the anterior margin in one focus  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  There are scattered tumor cells singly and in small groups  with adjacent ductal carcinoma in situ  The invasive tumor cells appear moderately differentiated  but they are few in number  which compromises accurate grading  Focally  the cytoplasm appears vacuolated or granular  The area of the carcinoma also contains aggregates of neutrophils and macrophages with adjacent dense fibrosis  The morphologic features of this tumor raise the possibility of treatment effect  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin highlight the tumor cells  Myoepithelial markers  p63  calponin  myosin  show that the tumor cells lack a myoepithelial envelope  while myoepithelial cells surround ductal carcinoma in situ  Macrophages stain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm oriented breast tissue with a needle localization wire in place and a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior   blue  posterior   black  medial   green  and lateral   yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm well circumscribed  white  fibrous mass  which abuts the medial  anterior  posterior  and inferior margins  and is 0 4cm from the lateral margin and 0 2cm from the superior margin  A hemorrhagic tract runs through the center of the mass  The specimen is entirely submitted from superior to inferior as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with both end margins submitted radially  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells are few in number and cannot be identified with certainty on the slide provided for FISH analysis  Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 23 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  CARCINOSARCOMA WITH FOCAL CARTILAGINOUS AND OSSEOUS DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is composed of both malignant epithelial and mesenchymal  sarcomatous  areas  These two components are distinct and do not show any merging from the carcinoma into the sarcoma  Immunoperoxidase stains confirm divergent differentiation  with cytokeratins being positive only in the epithelial areas and vimentin and desmin only in the sarcomatous regions  S 100 only stains the carcinoma  Although the differential diagnosis includes a metaplastic carcinoma with extensive sarcomatous areas  there is usually more blending of the epithelial and mesenchymal areas in metaplastic carcinoma  Also  immunoperoxidase usually shows some keratin positivity in the sarcomatous areas in a metaplastic carcinoma  Another interesting feature in this case is that the background of this tumor is reminiscent of a phylloides tumor  with broad stromal fronds focally covered by malignant epithelium  This feature raises the possibility that this tumor is arising in a high grade phylloides  All margins are greater than 0 2cm  No angiolymphatic invasion is seen  Dr  Koerner has reviewed the case and agrees with this interpretation  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 15                                                                                     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION   The tumor size is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  see gross description   No lymph nodes were identified in the axillary tail  Sections taken from this region also do not reveal lymph nodes  Added by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  18 MAY 00 at 16 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm right modified radical mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm tan wrinkled skin ellipse and a 2 9cm symmetrical nipple areolar complex  A short suture designates superior and long suture designates the axillary tail per the surgeon  There is a 5 5cm well healed curvilinear scar approximately 5 0cm lateral to the areola  The specimen is inked black and serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm well demarcated tan red  focally necrotic mass which comes within 2 7cm of the posterior margin of resection  closest margin  and approximately 0 5cm from the skin  Approximately 1 5cm superior posterior to the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm area of skin wedge  The posterior margin is retracted  Sectioning of this area reveals tan white fibrous tissue  A mass cannot grossly be identified in this area  The remaining breast tissue reveals approximately 65  yellow adipose tissue and 35  tan white unremarkable fibrous stroma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail is present containing no definite lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A D  Tumor  E  Posterior resection margin adjacent to tumor  F  Posterior margin  area of retraction  G  Random breast tissue  H J  Possible lymph nodes from axillary tail  Gross Description by  DELIA FINNIE Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Danielle D Elliott  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
