 beyond the mass of high grade carcinoma  and is present at the inferior  superior  posterior  and anterior margins of the specimen  Dr  F  Koerner has reviewed selected slides and concurs with the diagnosis of atypical microglandular adenosis  BREAST  RIGHT  POSTERIOR LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION  ATYPICAL MICROGLANDULAR ADENOSIS  PRESENT AT THE TRUE TISSUE MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  heavy chain myosin  p63  and calponin highlight the presence of myoepithelial cells  The lobular carcinoma cells are negative for e cadherin  BREAST  RIGHT  INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  ATYPICAL MICROGLANDULAR ADENOSIS  PRESENT AT THE TRUE TISSUE MARGIN BREAST  RIGHT  MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  MYXOID FIBROADENOMA  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT  SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimens were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross descriptions  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL     REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right sentinel node biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink to yellow nodular tissue consisting of a lymph node with attached adipose tissue  The surrounding fat is removed and the lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast lumpectomy   is a 