Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 00 CLINICAL DATA  32 year old female with a 2 6cm  grade 3 out of 3  ERPR positive breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASS    RE EXCISION  RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FAVOR LOBULAR TYPE  MULTIFOCAL ON 4 OF 4 SECTIONS  THE LARGEST NODULE REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF A CAUTERIZED POSTERIOR  DEEP  MARGIN  E   SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The tumor is most consistent with a lobular carcinoma  Neither an in situ lobular nor ductal component is identified  Slides from the previous excision are not available for comparison  No lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL INFEROLATERAL MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO NEW INFEROLATERAL MARGIN  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL LATERAL TISSUE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  ONE FOCUS WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF A CAUTERIZED MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH MILD DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA WITHIN 4 OF 15 LYMPH NODES  WITHOUT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  THE LARGEST NODE IS REMOVED_DATE CM AND REPLACED BY TUMOR   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL TISSUE    BIOPSY  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SINGLE NODE   WITHOUT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   LEVEL 3   BIOPSY  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  REPLACING A REMOVED_DATE CM NODE  WITHOUT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional inferolateral margin  is a 2 x 2 x 1cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue inked black and over inked green at the new inferolateral margin  Representative section frozen as FX  1  now in A  Remainder of tissue submitted in B and C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 5 x 4 x 1 5cm oriented fragment of breast tissue inked as follows  anterior and posterior  black  superior and lateral  green  and inferolateral  red  inferomedial  blue  superomedial  yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED