ology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 08 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm right modified radical mastectomy with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  A short black stitch designates the superior  and a long black stitch the lateral margins  The specimen is partially surfaced along the anterior aspect by a REMOVED_DATE x 11 0cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric 5 4cm areola  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unremarkable nipple which comes to 5 0cm of the superior margin  The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a poorly delineated  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  indurated  multinodular lesion  which comes to 6 5cm of the deep margin and is surrounded by focally cystic dense gray white fibrous tissue in the upper outer quadrant  The remaining cut surface shows diffusely nodular and cystic dense gray white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesion or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals numerous probable tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A   Deep margin closest to indurated lesion  en face   B C  Indurated lesion  entirely submitted from medial to lateral  D E  Representative fibrous tissue submitted from lateral to medial  F J  Possible lymph nodes  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SGR                                             