ubmitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 14   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 34 23PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  Posterior Medial  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The microinvasive tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The microinvasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The microinvasive tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Both microinvasive and ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells are negative for estrogen receptor protein and show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Focally  some ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells show faint staining for progesterone receptor protein  Breast  Left  Anterior Inferior  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  Some ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 26 24PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  Posterior Medial  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  The microinvasive tumor cells are not reliably identified on the slide examined by HER 2 FISH  Signal counts were obtained from the ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells  which also show HER 2 protein overexpression  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  826  to chromosome 17 signals  99  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 36 18PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left Posterior Medial   Core biopsy PART B  Breast  Left Anterior Inferior   Core biopsy  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  RAD Mammography Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  CONNIE ROCHE  NP Resident  Russell Ryan  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 59 year old woman with two left breast mass lesions  Lesion  1  specimen  A   is a BIRADS 5 on mammogram and U S and is located at 4 00 o clock  Lesion  2  specimen  B   is a 3 to 4cm heterogeneous mass on U S at 1 o clock  possibly a fibroadenoma  located at 1 00 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  see note   NOTE  The tumor is composed of large cells with abundant cytoplasm and fairly low nuclear to cytoplasmic ratio  The nuclei have irregular contours and hyperchromatic vesicular chromatin with prominent nucleoli  To confirm the diagnosis  we performed a panel of immunostains with the following results  STAIN TARGET RESULT E cadherin Ductal differentiation Positive Cytokeratin Epithelial cells Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Epithelial subset Positive CDX 2 GI epithelium Negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Macrophages Negative TTF 1 Lung Thyroid Negative Vimentin Renal cell CA Negative The immunoperoxidase staining pattern supports the morphologic findings and overall  the findings are compatible with invasive ductal carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  1 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  BENIGN BREAST PARENCHYMA WITH HYALINIZED STROMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  see note   NOTE  The findings may not correlate with the clinical impression of a mass lesion  Clinical correlation to ensure adequate sampling of the targeted lesion is suggested  Multiple levels were examined  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left breast  1 of 2  4 o clock   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  breast 1 o clock  2 of 2   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT  4 00   CORE BIOPSY  2  report_end  , Unchecked.
