Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 48 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old female with a mass on mammogram of the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  GREATER THAN 1 CM FROM THE CLOSEST RESECTION MARGIN  THE GROSS DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED   SEE NOTE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SECTION J   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Blood  vascular or lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a localization wire  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm  ill defined  hard  tan nodule away from an inked margin  A large hematoma and scattered areas of firmer  tan tissue are also present  The entire nodule and the adjacent margin is submitted in A through C  Representative sections of the hematoma and remaining firm tan tissue are submitted in cassettes D through J  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
