rs by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm nodular piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a firm  gritty  stellate white tan region extending to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the nodule is submitted in A through L  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO RESECTION MARGINS  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Checked.
